<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates · Immigration" title="Important changes to Spain’s Immigration Regulation in 2026" description="Royal Decree 316/2026 changed several immigration rules, so the current wording and the applicant’s dates matter." primaryLabel="Review my situation" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Immigration services" secondaryHref="/en/immigration" note="Published: April 2026 · Primary source: BOE." />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What changed</h2><p>Royal Decree 316/2026 amended Spain’s Immigration Regulation, including rules relevant to certain residence authorisations, regularisation and family members of Spanish citizens.</p><h2>Why older articles can mislead</h2><p>Guidance written under an earlier version may no longer reflect the current requirements. Any application should be checked against the current regulation and the applicant’s facts.</p><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/eli/es/rd/2026/04/14/316" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Royal Decree 316/2026 at the BOE →</a></p></div></section><CTA title="Has the applicable rule changed for your case?" text="Tell us what changed and we will start from the current regulation and relevant dates." label="Contact the firm" /></Layout>
